  <acqinfo id="d066e561f018cd599e4009078064560e">
    <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition</head>
<p>Ford Foundation archive was deposited at RAC in 2011. Ford Foundation records, correspondence, reports, program files and officers papers were transferred to, and accessioned by, RAC beginning in 2011. Accessions continue as necessary.</p><p>The Art Purchase Program files were gifted to the Ford Foundation archives by Melinda A. Agsten, Executrix of the Estate of Jane T. Ritchie, Andrew Ritchie's wife, in 1985.</p>  </acqinfo>
  <accessrestrict id="48a6c3790bb071edc3c069c03d045c1a">
    <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
<p>Records more than 10 years old are open for research. Brittle or damaged items are available at the discretion of RAC</p>  </accessrestrict>
  <bioghist id="1682d2ebe7a5044377a8614cb9f4f431">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>In March 1966 the Ford Foundation appointed Andrew Carnduff Ritchie (1907-1978), Director of the Yale University Art Gallery, as a consultant to select and purchase works of art for the Foundation's new headquarters building in New York City.  The appointment was to last approximately one year.</p><p>Ritchie's career included positions as Director, Albright Art Gallery (now, Albright-Knox Gallery) from 1942-1949; Director of the Painting and Sculpture Department, Museum of Modern Art from 1949-1957, and Director, Yale University Art Gallery from 1957-1971. During World War II Ritchie served with the celebrated "Monuments Men" in the Monuments, Fine Arts, and Archives (MFAA) section of the U.S. Army, as a representative of the Commanding General in Austria. </p><p>See also the Andrew Carnduff Ritchie papers in the Archives of American Art: http://www.aaa.si.edu/collections/andrew-carnduff-ritchie-papers-8152 .</p>  </bioghist>
  <arrangement id="574d2403beeac2a59dcd2778562d55fc">
    <head>Arrangement</head>
<p>Arranged in 4 series:  1. Administrative files;  2. Index to artists and artworks;  3. Dealer files;  4. Photographs of artworks.</p>  </arrangement>
  <scopecontent id="88bdd511c7b308067bf0c93388b2db5d">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>Consists of administrative files, dealer files, artist indexes and photos.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <relatedmaterial id="7dc8d019c38f54231e68d202267d4c74">
    <head>Related Materials</head>
<p>Ford Foundation Art Purchase Program files likely maintained by the Ford Foundation's Building Services department can be accessed here: FA1723, Ford Foundation records, Building Services, Ford Foundation artwork photographs</p>  </relatedmaterial>
  <userestrict id="5d42e05cfe2ea47107b5f8162222b4c2">
    <head>Conditions Governing Use</head>
<p>Ford Foundation has title, copyright and literary rights in the collection, in so far as it holds them.</p><p>The Rockefeller Archive Center has authority to grant permission to cite and publish material from the collection. Permission to publish extensive excerpts, or material in its entirety, will be referred to the Ford Foundation.</p>  </userestrict>
